 {"id":"DF-SPECLANG-025","title":"P1 DF-SPECLANG-023's premise is wrong: the clean-box tests-cell red is a harness artifact (npm ci --ignore-scripts ⇒ no better-sqlite3 binding), and the same clone is green (2071 passed, 0 failed) on the documented install path","status":"pending","priority":"P1","complexity":2,"capability_tags":["qa-harness","install-leg","testing","board-integrity"],"depends_on":["DF-SPECLANG-023"],"type":null,"created_at":"2026-11-20T08:52:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-20T08:52:00Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"8760715e4eef2cef5ea564db5dcb6b74af8985ff06581a676faf0a1704857049","source":"dogfood tick speclang-dogfood-2026-11-20-06-01-48 (install leg, bunker-mvp agent 1f93834b)","evidence":".coding-hermes/evidence/speclang-dogfood-2026-11-20-06-01-48/install-leg-tests-cell-rootcause.md"},"reasoning":"WHAT I RAN. The install leg executed for real this tick: bunker-qa.sh launch /home/kara/.hermes/cache/scratch/speclang-qa-c2 --server bunker-mvp on agent 1f93834b (a full git clone detached at upstream head c0dd9906, npm 10.9.8). Cells: toolchain-bootstrap OK x8, fresh-install OK, lint OK, tests FAIL, docker_build N/A, compose_config N/A. So no SKIPPED-install-bunker row is warranted.\n\nWHAT THE CELL ACTUALLY SAID (agent log ~/qa-logs-1012287/tests.log, summary verbatim):\n  Test Files  15 failed | 112 passed | 4 skipped (131)\n        Tests  86 failed | 1985 passed | 58 skipped (2129)\nThat is 15 files and 86 tests, not the single cli.test.ts failure DF-SPECLANG-023 records.\n\nROOT CAUSE, QUOTED. `grep -ac 'Could not locate the bindings' ~/qa-logs-1012287/tests.log` = 53. Every one of the 15 files is on the better-sqlite3 path (db.test.ts, db/migrations, db/cascades-migration, db/corrupt-state-*, db/ralph-loop-*, mcp.test.ts, mcp/bin-path, mcp/mcp-status-corrupt-db, cli/history, cli.test.ts's index tests, examples/hello-world-verification, ci/ci005-precommit-hook). The binding was never built because the harness suppresses dependency install scripts:\n  bunker-qa.sh:891  DETECT_INSTALL=\"npm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund\"\n  bunker-qa.sh:894  (same, for the two-package case)\nbetter-sqlite3's install script (prebuild-install || node-gyp rebuild --release) is exactly what --ignore-scripts removes, so node_modules/better-sqlite3/build/Release/better_sqlite3.node never exists. This is NOT the npm>=12 allowScripts issue the README documents: that agent runs npm 10.9.8, where the approval model does not apply.\n\nTHREE-REGIME PROOF (all at c0dd9906; product tree identical to 69abf2ab):\n 1. bunker, npm ci --ignore-scripts, npm test (serial) -> 15 files / 86 tests red, 53 binding errors.\n 2. local clone speclang-qa-c3, npm 12.2.3, npm ci --ignore-scripts (same flag reproduced) -> 12 files / 79 tests red, 53 binding errors, no build/ directory.\n 3. local clone speclang-qa-c4, npm 12.2.3, plain npm ci (the README path) -> node_modules/better-sqlite3/build/Release/better_sqlite3.node present, `npm run check:sqlite-binding` = 'OK: better-sqlite3 native binding loads (SELECT 1 -> {\"x\":1})', and `npm test` (pretest build + parallel vitest) = GREEN: Test Files 127 passed | 4 skipped (131), Tests 2071 passed | 58 skipped (2129), exit 0, Duration 28.72s.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS. Left alone, a worker wave is spent chasing 86 phantom product failures, the QA lane keeps publishing a red that says nothing about specLang, and the real green of the documented path is invisible. The tests cell currently measures the harness, not the repo.\n\nWHAT IS *NOT* A FINDING (recorded so nobody re-derives it): running `npx vitest run` without `pretest`/`npm run build` (no dist/) reddens 9 files / 35 tests that load dist/src/pipeline/executor.js, and tests/cli.test.ts > index > should refresh index with --refresh fails 3x (retry x2) in that regime and passes in the documented one. Both are the same instrumentation family.","foreman_note":"This row corrects DF-SPECLANG-023 rather than duplicating it: 023's AC premise (one cli.test.ts failure